{
  "title": "52: al-Toor الطور",
  "code": "012",
  "data": "بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمٰنِ الرَّحِيْمِ\nBISMIL LAAHIR RAHMAANIR RAHEEM\nIn the Name of Allah, the All-merciful, the All-compassionate\nوَالطُّوْرِۙ‏(1)\nWA TOORE.\nBy the Mount (of Revelation); \nوَكِتٰبٍ مَّسْطُوْرٍۙ‏(2)\nWA KETAABIM MMASTOORIN.\nBy a Decree inscribed \nفِىْ رَقٍّ مَّنْشُوْرٍۙ‏(3)\nFEE RAQQIN MMANSHOORIN.\nIn a Scroll unfolded; \nوَالْبَيْتِ الْمَعْمُوْرِۙ‏(4)\nWA BAYTE AL-MAA’MOORE.\nBy the much-frequented Fane; \nوَالسَّقْفِ الْمَرْفُوْعِۙ‏(5)\nWAALSSAQFE AL-MARFOOE’E.\nBy the Canopy Raised High; \nوَالْبَحْرِ الْمَسْجُوْرِۙ‏(6)\nWAL BAHRE AL-MASJOORE.\nAnd by the Ocean filled with Swell;- \nاِنَّ عَذَابَ رَبِّكَ لوَاقِعٌ ۙ‏(7)\nINNAL A’ZAABAL RABBEKA LWAAQEA’UN.\nVerily, the Doom of thy Lord will indeed come to pass;- \nمَّا لَهٗ مِنْ دَافِعٍۙ‏(8)\nMAA LAHU MIN DAAFEA’IN.\nThere is none can avert it;- \nيَّوْمَ تَمُوْرُ السَّمَآءُ مَوْرًا ۙ‏(9)\nYAWMA TAMOORO SAMAAA-O MAWRAN.\nOn the Day when the firmament will be in dreadful commotion. \nوَّتَسِيْرُ الْجِبَالُ سَيْرًا ؕ‏(10)\nWWATASEERU JEBAALO SAYRAN.\nAnd the mountains will fly hither and thither. \nفَوَيْلٌ يَّوْمَئِذٍ لِّلْمُكَذِّبِيْنَۙ‏(11)\nLAHUM YAWMA-EZIN LIL-MOKAZZEBEENAL.\nThen woe that Day to those that treat (Truth) as Falsehood;- \nالَّذِيْنَ هُمْ فِىْ خَوْضٍ يَّلْعَبُوْنَۘ‏(12)\nLAZEENA HUM FEE KHAWZIN YAL-A’BOON.\nThat play (and paddle) in shallow trifles. \nيَوْمَ يُدَعُّوْنَ اِلٰى نَارِ جَهَنَّمَ دَعًّاؕ‏(13)\nYAWMA YUDAUU’OONA ELAA NAARE JAHANNAMA DAAA’AN.\nThat Day shall they be thrust down to the Fire of Hell, irresistibly. \nهٰذِهِ النَّارُ الَّتِىْ كُنْتُمْ بِهَا تُكَذِّبُوْنَ‏(14)\nHAAZEHE TAMASSANAN LATEE KUNTUM BEHAA TOKAZZEBOON.\n“This:, it will be said, “Is the Fire, which ye were wont to deny! \nاَفَسِحْرٌ هٰذَاۤ اَمْ اَنْتُمْ لَا تُبْصِرُوْنَۚ‏(15)\nAAFASEHRUN HAAZAA AM ANTUM LAA TUBSEROON.\n“Is this then a fake, or is it ye that do not see? \nاِصْلَوْهَا فَاصْبِرُوْۤا اَوْ لَا تَصْبِرُوْاۚ سَوَآءٌ عَلَيْكُمْؕ اِنَّمَا تُجْزَوْنَ مَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَ‏(16)\nISLAWHAL FAASBEROOA AW LAA TASBEROOA SAWAAA-UN A’LAYKUM INNAMAA TUJZAWNA MAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\n“Burn ye therein: the same is it to you whether ye bear it with patience, or not: Ye but receive the recompense of your (own) deeds.” \nاِنَّ الْمُتَّقِيْنَ فِىْ جَنّٰتٍ وَّنَعِيْمٍۙ‏(17)\nINNAL MA-A’L MUTTAQEEN FEE JANNAATIN WWANAE’EEMIN.\nAs to the Righteous, they will be in Gardens, and in Happiness, \nفٰكِهِيْنَ بِمَاۤ اٰتٰٮهُمْ رَبُّهُمْۚ وَوَقٰٮهُمْ رَبُّهُمْ عَذَابَ الْجَحِيْمِ‏(18)\nFAAKEHEENA BEMAA AAATAAHUM RABBOHUM WA WAQAAHUM RABBOHUM A’ZAABAL JAHEEM.\nEnjoying the (Bliss) which their Lord hath bestowed on them, and their Lord shall deliver them from the Penalty of the Fire. \nكُلُوْا وَاشْرَبُوْا هَنِٓيْئًا ۢ بِمَا كُنْتُمْ تَعْمَلُوْنَۙ‏(19)\nKOLOO WASH RABOO HANEEEAN BEMAA KUNTUM TA’MALOON.\n(To them will be said:) “Eat and drink ye, with profit and health, because of your (good) deeds.” \nمُتَّكِئِيْنَ عَلٰى سُرُرٍ مَّصْفُوْفَةٍ ۚ وَزَوَّجْنٰهُمْ بِحُوْرٍ عِيْنٍ‏(20)\nMUTTAKE-EENA A’LAA SORORIM MMASFOOFATIN WA ZAWWAJNAAHUM BE-HOORIN E’EENIN.\nThey will recline (with ease) on Thrones (of dignity) arranged in ranks; and We shall join them to Companions, with beautiful big and lustrous eyes. \nوَالَّذِيْنَ اٰمَنُوْا وَاتَّبَعَتْهُمْ ذُرِّيَّتُهُمْ بِاِيْمَانٍ اَلْحَقْنَا بِهِمْ ذُرِّيَّتَهُمْ وَمَاۤ اَلَتْنٰهُمْ مِّنْ عَمَلِهِمْ مِّنْ شَىْءٍؕ كُلُّ امْرِیءٍۢ بِمَا كَسَبَ رَهِيْنٌ‏(21)\nWAL LAZEENA AAMANOO WAATTABAA’ATHUM ZURREETUHUM BEAEEMAANIN AALHAQNAA BEHIM ZURRIYYATAHUM WA MAA AALATNAAHUM MIN A’AMALEHEM MIN SHAYIN KULLO RE-IM BEMAA KASABA RAHEENUN.\nAnd those who believe and whose families follow them in Faith, to them shall We join their families: Nor shall We deprive them (of the fruit) of aught of their works: (Yet) is each individual in pledge for his deeds. \nوَاَمْدَدْنٰهُمْ بِفَاكِهَةٍ وَّلَحْمٍ مِّمَّا يَشْتَهُوْنَ‏(22)\nWAAMDADNAAHUM BE-FAAKEHATIN WWALAHMIN MIMMAA YASHTAHOONA.\nAnd We shall bestow on them, of fruit and meat, anything they shall desire. \nيَتَنَازَعُوْنَ فِيْهَا كَاْسًا لَّا لَغْوٌ فِيْهَا وَلَا تَاْثِيْمٌ‏(23)\nYATANAAZAU’OONA FEEHAA KA’SAN LAA LAGHWUN FEEHAA WA LAA TAASEEMUN.\nThey shall there exchange, one with another, a (loving) cup free of frivolity, free of all taint of ill. \nوَيَطُوْفُ عَلَيْهِمْ غِلْمَانٌ لَّهُمْ كَاَنَّهُمْ لُؤْلُؤٌ مَّكْنُوْنٌ‏(24)\nWA YATOOFO A’LAYHIM GHELMAANUN LAHUM KA-ANNAHUM LULUUN MMAKNOONUN.\nRound about them will serve, (devoted) to them, young male servants (handsome) as Pearls well-guarded. \nوَاَقْبَلَ بَعْضُهُمْ عَلٰى بَعْضٍ يَّتَسَآءَلُوْنَ‏(25)\nWAAQBALA KHALAA A’LAA ELAA YYATASAAALOONA.\nThey will advance to each other, engaging in mutual enquiry. \nقَالُوْۤا اِنَّا كُنَّا قَبْلُ فِىْۤ اَهْلِنَا مُشْفِقِيْنَ‏(26)\nQAALOO INNAA KUNNAA QABLO FEE AAHLENAA MUSHFEQEENA.\nThey will say: “Aforetime, we were not without fear for the sake of our people. \nفَمَنَّ اللّٰهُ عَلَيْنَا وَوَقٰٮنَا عَذَابَ السَّمُوْمِ‏(27)\nFAMANNA LAAHO A’LAYNAA WAWAQAANAA A’ZAABAL AS-SAMOOME.\n“But Allah has been good to us, and has delivered us from the Penalty of the Scorching Wind. \nاِنَّا كُنَّا مِنْ قَبْلُ نَدْعُوْهُ ؕ اِنَّهٗ هُوَ الْبَرُّ الرَّحِيْمُ‏(28)\nINNAA KUNNAA MIN QABLO NADU’OOHU INNAHU HOWA AL-BARRU RAHEEM.\n“Truly, we did call unto Him from of old: truly it is He, the Beneficent, the Merciful!” \nفَذَكِّرْ فَمَاۤ اَنْتَ بِنِعْمَتِ رَبِّكَ بِكَاهِنٍ وَّلَا مَجْنُوْنٍؕ‏(29)\nFA-ZAKKIR FAMAA ANTA BENEA’MATE RABBEKA BEKAAHENIN WA LAA MAJNOONIN.\nTherefore proclaim thou the praises (of thy Lord): for by the Grace of thy Lord, thou art no (vulgar) soothsayer, nor art thou one possessed. \nاَمْ يَقُوْلُوْنَ شَاعِرٌ نَّتَرَبَّصُ بِهٖ رَيْبَ الْمَنُوْنِ‏(30)\nAM YAQOOLOONA SHAAE’ERUN NNATARABBASU BEHI RAYBA AL-MANOONE.\nOr do they say:- “A Poet! we await for him some calamity (hatched) by Time!” \nقُلْ تَرَبَّصُوْا فَاِنِّىْ مَعَكُمْ مِّنَ الْمُتَرَبِّصِيْنَ ؕ‏(31)\nQUL TARABBASOOA FA-INNEE MA-A’KUM MENAL AL-MUTARABBESEENA.\nSay thou: “Await ye!- I too will wait along with you!” \nاَمْ تَاْمُرُهُمْ اَحْلَامُهُمْ بِهٰذَآ اَمْ هُمْ قَوْمٌ طَاغُوْنَۚ‏(32)\nAM TAAMURUHUM AAHLAAMUHUM BEHAAZAA AM HUM QAWMUN TAAGHOONA.\nIs it that their faculties of understanding urge them to this, or are they but a people transgressing beyond bounds? \nاَمْ يَقُوْلُوْنَ تَقَوَّلَهٗ ۚ بَلْ لَّا يُؤْمِنُوْنَ ۚ‏(33)\nAM YAQOOLOONA TAQAWLAH BAL LAA YOAMENOONA.\nOr do they say, “He fabricated the (Message)”? Nay, they have no faith! \nفَلْيَاْتُوْا بِحَدِيْثٍ مِّثْلِهٖۤ اِنْ كَانُوْا صٰدِقِيْنَؕ‏(34)\nFALYAATOOA BEHADEESIN MISLEH IN KAANOO SAADEQEENA.\nLet them then produce a recital like unto it, If (it be) they speak the truth! \nاَمْ خُلِقُوْا مِنْ غَيْرِ شَىْءٍ اَمْ هُمُ الْخٰلِقُوْنَؕ‏(35)\nAM KHULEQOOA MIN GHAIRE SHAY-IN AM HOMUL AL-KHAALEQOONA.\nWere they created of nothing, or were they themselves the creators? \nاَمْ خَلَقُوا السَّمٰوٰتِ وَالْاَرْضَۚ بَلْ لَّا يُوْقِنُوْنَؕ‏(36)\nAM KHALAQOOA SAMAAWAATE WAL ARZA BAL LAA YOOQENOON.\nOr did they create the heavens and the earth? Nay, they have no firm belief. \nاَمْ عِنْدَهُمْ خَزَآئِنُ رَبِّكَ اَمْ هُمُ الْمُصَۜيْطِرُوْنَؕ‏(37)\nAM E’ENDAHUM KHAZAAENUS RABBEKA AM HOMUL AL-MUSAYTEROONA.\nOr are the Treasures of thy Lord with them, or are they the managers (of affairs)? \nاَمْ لَهُمْ سُلَّمٌ يَّسْتَمِعُوْنَ فِيْهِ ۚ فَلْيَاْتِ مُسْتَمِعُهُمْ بِسُلْطٰنٍ مُّبِيْنٍؕ‏(38)\nAM LAHUM SULLAMUN YYASTAMEU’OONA FEEHE FALYAATE MUSTAMEU’UHUM BESULTAANIM MMUBEENIN.\nOr have they a ladder, by which they can (climb up to heaven and) listen (to its secrets)? Then let (such a) listener of theirs produce a manifest proof. \nاَمْ لَهُ الْبَنٰتُ وَلَكُمُ الْبَنُوْنَؕ‏(39)\nAM LAHUL AL-BANAATU WA LAKOMUL AL-BANOONA.\nOr has He only daughters and ye have sons? \nاَمْ تَسْئَلُهُمْ اَجْرًا فَهُمْ مِّنْ مَّغْرَمٍ مُّثْقَلُوْنَؕ‏(40)\nAM TASALUHUM AJRAN FAHUM MIN MMAGHRAMIN MMUSQALOONA.\nOr is it that thou dost ask for a reward, so that they are burdened with a load of debt? \nاَمْ عِنْدَهُمُ الْغَيْبُ فَهُمْ يَكْتُبُوْنَؕ‏(41)\nAM E’ENDAHUMU AL-GHAYBU FAHUM YAKTUBOONA.\nOr that the Unseen in it their hands, and they write it down? \nاَمْ يُرِيْدُوْنَ كَيْدًاؕ فَالَّذِيْنَ كَفَرُوْا هُمُ الْمَكِيْدُوْنَؕ‏(42)\nAM YOREEDOONA KAYDAN FAL LAZEENA KAFAROO HOMUL AL-MAKEEDOONA.\nOr do they intend a plot (against thee)? But those who defy Allah are themselves involved in a Plot! \nاَمْ لَهُمْ اِلٰهٌ غَيْرُ اللّٰهِؕ سُبْحٰنَ اللّٰهِ عَمَّا يُشْرِكُوْنَ‏(43)\nAM LAHUM ELAAHUN GHAYRO LAAH LAAHE LAAHE A’MMAA YUSHREKOON.\nOr have they a god other than Allah? Exalted is Allah far above the things they associate with Him! \nوَاِنْ يَّرَوْا كِسْفًا مِّنَ السَّمَآءِ سَاقِطًا يَّقُوْلُوْا سَحَابٌ مَّرْكُوْمٌ‏(44)\nWA YYARAWA KESFAN MENAL SAMAAA-E SAAQETAN YAQOOLOO SAHAABUN MMARKOOMUN.\nWere they to see a piece of the sky falling (on them), they would (only) say: “Clouds gathered in heaps!” \nفَذَرْهُمْ حَتّٰى يُلٰقُوْا يَوْمَهُمُ الَّذِىْ فِيْهِ يُصْعَقُوْنَۙ‏(45)\nFAZARHUM HATTAA YULAAQOOA YAWMAHUMU LAZEE FEEHE YUSA’AQOONA.\nSo leave them alone until they encounter that Day of theirs, wherein they shall (perforce) swoon (with terror), \nيَوْمَ لَا يُغْنِىْ عَنْهُمْ كَيْدُهُمْ شَيْئًا وَّلَا هُمْ يُنْصَرُوْنَؕ‏(46)\nYAWMA LAA YUGHNEE A’NHUM KAYDUHUM SHAY-ANW WA LAA HUM YUNSAROON.\nThe Day when their plotting will avail them nothing and no help shall be given them. \nوَاِنَّ لِلَّذِيْنَ ظَلَمُوْا عَذَابًا دُوْنَ ذٰلِكَ وَلٰكِنَّ اَكْثَرَهُمْ لَا يَعْلَمُوْنَ‏(47)\nWA INNA LILLAZEENA ZALAMOO A’ZAABAN DOONA ZAALEKA LAAKINNAL AKSARAHUM LAA YA’LAMOON.\nAnd verily, for those who do wrong, there is another punishment besides this: But most of them understand not. \nوَاصْبِرْ لِحُكْمِ رَبِّكَ فَاِنَّكَ بِاَعْيُنِنَا وَسَبِّحْ بِحَمْدِ رَبِّكَ حِيْنَ تَقُوْمُۙ‏(48)\nWAS BIR LE HUKME RABBEKA FA-INNAKA BEAAA’YUNENAA WASABBEH BE-HAMDE RABBEKA HEENA YAQOOMUS.\nNow await in patience the command of thy Lord: for verily thou art in Our eyes: and celebrate the praises of thy Lord the while thou standest forth, \nوَمِنَ الَّيْلِ فَسَبِّحْهُ وَاِدْبَارَ النُّجُوْمِ‏(49)\nWA MENAN LAYLE FASABBEHHU WAADBAARA NOJOOM.\nAnd for part of the night also praise thou Him, and at the retreat of the stars!",
  "merits": "Surah al-Toor (The Mountain)\nThis Surah has 49 verses and it was revealed in Makkah. The Holy Prophet (s.a.w.a.) said that the one who recites this Surah will be kept safe from the wrath and punishment of Allah (s.w.t.).\nImam Ja’far al-Sadiq (a.s.) has said that the recitation of this Surah brings good fortune to the reciter and constant recitation by those who have been imprisoned secures an early release from bondage. Surah al-Toor, if recited or kept as a talisman, keeps children in good health."
}
